Z||000006||Gold-86SE||05-16-2000||02:41 PM||||Hey Loafer, if that GT gets out of the family and you have an itchin' to drive a fiero, you will long for the ole days.  If it is not necessary to part with your Fiero, don't. Sooner or later you will have SELLER'S REMORSE, if you're not sure that is the opposite of BUYER'S REMORSE - which you might just get with that RICER of yours.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||05-16-2000||03:01 PM||||loafer, Nice car but listen to the others. I had an 86 SE bought new in 86, 5 years later I got rid of it. Then about 5 years ago a friend stopped by with his 85 coupe and I missed the Fiero so much that I bought another 86 SE and have been very happy since. If possible keep the GT and slowly restore it to showroom condition. Use the Miata as your daily driver. That way when the urge to cruise comes over you, hop into the Fiero and go! There has never been or ever be a car as unique as the Fiero!||||reg||6
